</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEJIMA, FUMIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEJIMA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEJIMA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEJIMA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An incinerator for removing noxious substances from a flue gas, characterized by comprising an incineration section adapted to burn an object material therein, a removal section adapted to remove noxious substances occurring in the incineration section and joined to the above section, and a suction vacuum means or an air supply vacuum means adapted to generate a flow of air advancing from the incineration section to the removal section, so as to keep the interior of the incineration section in a vacuum at all times.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un incinérateur destiné à éliminer des substances nocives provenant d'un gaz de combustion. Cet incinérateur comprend une section d'incinération conçue pour brûler un matériau, une section d'élimination conçue pour éliminer des substances nocives se formant dans la section d'incinération et reliée à la section précitée, et un dispositif d'aspiration ou un dispositif à vide d'alimentation en air conçu pour générer un flux d'air de la section d'incinération à la section d'élimination de façon à maintenir sous vide la section d'incinération.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title